=== the images: built from the declarations, and not booted ===
mirror_source: image built (19 expected lines)
mirror_keeper: image built (18 expected lines)
=== round 0: each machine booted alone makes its key and publishes the public half ===
enrolled: each device's key, as the line it printed on its own console
=== the roll: both enrolled, the copy named ===
roll: fleet boutique -- 2 members on lan, served by nobody in this fleet -- judged, no refusal
roll:   mirror ledger_copy -- depot gives /data/ledger to annex, which keeps it in /data/copy and asks every 5 s, in warehouse
roll:   depot -- mirror_source (mirror_source.machine, 10.30.0.1/24) -- 52:54:00:12:37:01 -- in shop -- enrolled, fingerprint FP1
roll:   annex -- mirror_keeper (mirror_keeper.machine, 10.30.0.2/24) -- 52:54:00:12:37:02 -- in warehouse -- enrolled, fingerprint FP2
=== the images again, from the enrolled declarations ===
mirror_source: image built (19 expected lines)
mirror_keeper: image built (18 expected lines)
mirror_keeper_plain: image built (18 expected lines)
=== round 1: declared -- the source holds a ledger, and the keeper asks for it ===
disk: round 1 -- the source's /data/ledger holds 3 files besides the note, 2 directories, 300060 bytes
disk: round 1 -- the keeper's /data/copy holds 3 files besides the note, 2 directories, 300060 bytes
disk: round 1 -- it is, file for file, the directory the source's disk holds: yes
disk: round 1 -- /data/copy.last says: ok files=4 dirs=2 bytes=300066
=== round 2: changed -- the directory changes while the machines are down, and the copy follows ===
disk: round 2 -- the source's /data/ledger holds 3 files besides the note, 2 directories, 300063 bytes
disk: round 2 -- the keeper's /data/copy holds 3 files besides the note, 2 directories, 300063 bytes
disk: round 2 -- it is, file for file, the directory the source's disk holds: yes
disk: round 2 -- the file the source removed is gone from the copy: yes
disk: round 2 -- the copy of round 1 and the copy of round 2 are the same directory: no
disk: round 2 -- /data/copy.last says: ok files=4 dirs=2 bytes=300069
=== round 3: an impostor -- a different machine answers from the source's address, with a ledger of its own ===
disk: round 3 -- the keeper's /data/copy is the copy it had before the impostor answered: yes
disk: round 3 -- the forged ledger reached the keeper's disk: no
disk: round 3 -- /data/copy.last says: unverified the listing was signed by somebody else than the source
=== round 4: a stranger -- a keeper that is not the device the source gives to asks for the ledger ===
disk: round 4 -- the stranger's disk holds a copy of the ledger: no
disk: round 4 -- /data/copy.last says: silent 10.30.0.1:7400 gave no listing
=== round 5: a link -- the world makes a symbolic link in its own directory, to the machine's password file ===
disk: round 5 -- the keeper's /data/copy is the copy it had: yes
disk: round 5 -- /data/copy.last says: refused stolen is a symbolic link: a copy holds files and directories, and a link is a way to somewhere else
=== round 6: a hard link -- the world makes a regular file in its own directory that is the machine's own device key ===
disk: round 6 -- the source's /data/ledger/mykey is the device key itself, under another name: yes
disk: round 6 -- the keeper's /data/copy is the copy it had: yes
disk: round 6 -- the source's device key is anywhere on the keeper's disk: no
disk: round 6 -- /data/copy.last says: refused mykey belongs to uid 0 and the world's is 2000: the floor gives only what the world owns
=== round 7: alone -- the source is gone, and what the keeper kept is the thing that is there ===
disk: round 7 -- the keeper's /data/copy is the copy it had: yes
disk: round 7 -- /data/copy.last says: silent nobody answered at 10.30.0.1:7400
=== round 8: the cut -- what a pull cut short left on the keeper's disk, and a boot after it ===
disk: round 8 -- before the boot the keeper's disk holds the staging place: yes, its record: yes
disk: round 8 -- after it the staging place is gone: yes, and so is the record that waited for it: yes
disk: round 8 -- the keeper's /data/copy is the copy it had: yes
=== round 8, again: the cut between the first two renames -- the copy set aside, the new one not yet in its place ===
disk: round 8 -- before the boot the keeper holds no /data/copy: yes, and holds the copy it set aside: yes
disk: round 8 -- after it the copy is back where it was, and is the copy it had: yes, and the set-aside name is gone: yes
=== round 9: tampered -- a file of the copy is changed on the keeper's disk, and nothing is there to heal it ===
disk: round 9 -- the witness convicted the copy: yes, and the machine's boot was judged to match its expectation: no
=== round 10: no disk -- the mount a copy lies on is refused by the kernel, and neither machine says what it cannot keep ===
disk: round 10 -- the source, with no disk, said it gives the ledger: no
disk: round 10 -- the keeper, with no disk, said it takes a copy: no
=== the host: the copy of round 1 and the copy of round 2, by somebody who holds only the fleet file ===
first: mirror: fleet boutique, MIRROR ledger_copy -- depot (enrolled as FP1) gives /data/ledger to annex (enrolled as FP2)
first: mirror: zig-out/mirror/k_r1/copy -- 4 files, 2 directories, 300066 bytes: every file matches the digest the source signed, and nothing else is there
first: mirror: the listing was signed by FP1 for FP2, the two keys this fleet holds, and no secret took part
first: exit 0
second: mirror: fleet boutique, MIRROR ledger_copy -- depot (enrolled as FP1) gives /data/ledger to annex (enrolled as FP2)
second: mirror: zig-out/mirror/k_r2/copy -- 4 files, 2 directories, 300069 bytes: every file matches the digest the source signed, and nothing else is there
second: mirror: the listing was signed by FP1 for FP2, the two keys this fleet holds, and no secret took part
second: exit 0
