no-disk source: the source, with no disk behind its mount:
srcnodisk: boot: harb init -- machine mirror_source (hosted / x86_64 / qemu_pc) -- pid 1
srcnodisk: boot: console /dev/ttyS0
srcnodisk: boot: mount proc at /proc -- done
srcnodisk: boot: mount sysfs at /sys -- done
srcnodisk: boot: mount devtmpfs at /dev -- done
srcnodisk: boot: mount ext4 at /data -- refused by the kernel: NOENT
srcnodisk: boot: grant process (effectful)
srcnodisk: boot: grant filesystem (effectful)
srcnodisk: boot: grant network (effectful)
srcnodisk: boot: network lan -- eth0 up 10.30.0.1/24
srcnodisk: boot: identity -- ed25519, custody a file at /data/device.key -- created on this device, fingerprint FP5
srcnodisk: boot: mirror -- this machine cannot give /data/ledger: the mount it lies on was refused by the kernel, and a world that was not given its directory has nothing to give
srcnodisk: boot: confine -- enrol has no network of its own, ledger has no network of its own and no sight of the other worlds and no way to start one; what a world did not declare, the kernel does not give it
srcnodisk: boot: floor -- the machine is not a world's to change: none may mount or unmount, set the clock, load a module, rename the host, make or enter a namespace, trace another process, take a priority over the other worlds, or reboot the box
srcnodisk: boot: state -- ledger was not given /data/ledger: the mount it lies on was refused by the kernel; a world that owns a directory it was not given does not start
srcnodisk: boot: start enrol -- pid N -- /harb attest --export
srcnodisk: attest mirror_source -- ed25519, fingerprint FP5
srcnodisk: enrol mirror_source ed25519 KEY5 -- KEY for this machine's MEMBER in a fleet
srcnodisk: attest: signed 21 bytes with this device's key and verified them against its public half
srcnodisk: attest: one bit flipped in the message, and the same signature is refused
srcnodisk: boot: enrol (pid N) exited 0
srcnodisk: boot: every service has ended -- init has nothing left to keep alive
srcnodisk: boot: init halts the machine -- reboot(RESTART)
srcnodisk: reboot: Restarting system
